{
  "$comment": "Per feed (feeds): each field required or optional, as the feed declares it (core/feed.h; tests/functional/feeds.test.mjs keeps them equal): a source that cannot fill an optional field leaves it at its placeholder and the component bound to it hides. Where each screen's data can come from (Settings > Screens; ported from the panel lab's screen catalogue). Per screen: shows (what the screen shows, in words: its settings page opens with it), needs (the equipment in words, null = every home), sources in order of preference. A source: id, kind (builtin = worked out on the panel, ha = a Home Assistant integration or entity domain, direct = the panel calls a service itself), name, detect (how a host's discovery finds it: integration and / or domain), setup (what a direct source needs first), fills (which screen parameters it fills: domain [+ integration] -> every matching entity (list: true, a comma list) or one). The host (the workbench, later a Home Assistant integration) runs discovery and writes the values into the panel's deck. Feeds (CONTRACT.md C51, 2026-10-29): feed = the panel.<feed> entity the screen binds; each source names the adapter that fills it (core/<feed>_source.cpp), set through the feeds settings of the spec.",
